bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27, 0, "Measured (base seed aa542919a298e130 = origin f43f68c218e, release/1.0.0, aarch64, JIT): fn g(x, k: i64) -> i64 with a nil match, called 4e8 times as g(Col.Red, 0) + g(raw, 0). Adding a never-taken branch 'if k > 5: val t = h(k, 1, 2) + ... + h(k, 30, 2); return t' raises wall time 1.10s -> 1.95s (+2.1 ns per call); moving the same 30 calls into a separate fn slow(x, k) called from that branch is flat (1.10-1.16s). The cranelift function pays prologue/frame (callee-saved spills) for every call it contains on every entry, even when the branch never runs."
    seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27, 1, "Repro: cold0.spl vs cold30.spl vs coldout.spl (30 h() calls inline in a dead branch vs outlined); alternate run order. Expected: a never-taken cold branch costs ~0 on the hot path (shrink-wrapping / cold-block outlining), so source does not have to outline by hand. Workaround in use: seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27 moved its registration path into one __erased_none_arm_slow_* helper per module."

